    [Test][Misc] Enable V2 model runner for GLM E2E test cases (#19500)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Migrate the existing GLM-5.3-W8A8C8-A3-200k-PP-PD nightly to explicit
    Model Runner V2 with PCP instead of legacy DSA CP. Prefill uses
    DP1/TP1/PCP16/PP2 across two hosts with layer partition42,36; both
    Prefill hosts use16NPUs. Update Mooncake Prefill TP metadata to1 on both
    P/D sides. Decode retains globalDP16/localDP8/TP2 across two
    hosts,16NPUs each: four hosts64NPUs in total.
    
    Align the launch configuration with the earlier8bf7fe69 TP2/PCP8 run,
    changing only Prefill TP2/PCP8 toTP1/PCP16 and the corresponding
    Mooncake TP metadata. Restore Prefill max-num-batched-tokens16384,
    gpu-memory-utilization0.92 and HCCL_BUFFSIZE2560MiB; Decode
    remains256/0.92/1024MiB. Model, int8KV/indexer, MTP1P/MTP5D, graph
    modes,16K input dataset, benchmark settings/baselines and trigger stay
    unchanged.
    
    Retain the optional, unregistered
    GLM-5.2-W8A8C8-A3_128k-static-super-kernels.yaml migration: explicit V2,
    globalDP8/localDP4, TP1/PCP4 on both hosts, HCCL_BUFFSIZE768, no legacy
    DSA CP; static/super kernels, MLAPO,MTP3 and benchmarks remain
    unchanged. No new matrix entry is added.
    
    The A3 Flash130k PD migration is isolated in #20108. No A5 or shared
    workflow changes are included.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. Nightly/test configuration changes only.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Latest adjustment (`893a29f2a`): increase only both PP-PD Prefill HCCL
    buffers from2048 to2560MiB. Decode stays1024, P TP1/PCP16/PP2,
    batched16384/memory0.92, GLM-5.2 and benchmarks are unchanged. The
    DispatchFFNCombine formula gives2314MiB for M16384/K6144/topK8,
    leaving246MiB margin. Actual M was not printed in run40675402391, whose
    Prefill profile failed with EZ1008 tiling; buffer insufficiency is still
    a hypothesis. Loader/all-rank environment checks, semantic comparison
    and diff check passed. Full formatting blocked by missing local
    pre-commit; NPU validation pending and no nightly triggered.
    
    - Compared the full GLM YAML against the8bf7fe69 configuration: the only
    semantic differences are Prefill TP2/PCP8 ->TP1/PCP16 and matching
    Mooncake Prefill TP metadata. Preserved all Decode options and benchmark
    dictionaries.
    - Loaded with repository ExternalDPConfigLoader, resolved18ranks and
    rendered every ServerCommandBuilder command. Confirmed four16NPU hosts,
    P TP1/PCP16/PP2, batched16384/memory0.92/buffer2560 and consistent
    embedded JSON/PD metadata. Diff whitespace checks passed.
    - Restored optional GLM-5.2 exactly to its pre-removal configuration;
    YAML/embedded JSON checks passed. Prior parser checks verified localDP4
    x TP1 x PCP4=16NPUs/host.
    - bash format.sh ci attempted; full formatting blocked by unavailable
    local pre-commit.
    - Earlier TP2/PCP8 runtime evidence (Ascend8bf7fe69/vLLMdb9527a):
    runs40431203121 and40440760810 completed96/96 performance requests and
    AIME30/30 with826.5579/819.2133token/s, below baseline877.3186 x0.97.
    This does not validate the newTP1/PCP16 configuration or current
    vLLM0.32.0.
    - Recent TP1/PCP8 attempts failed before benchmarking:16K/0.90 profile
    OOM;8K/0.90 reported available KV memory -3.42GiB and no memory for
    cache blocks. These are different configurations and do not establish
    the result of the current target.
    - Synced upstream main02ac27a19 in0fd470507, including upstream
    vLLM0.32.0 import compatibility. Fresh NPU four-host PP/PD startup,
    performance and accuracy validation is pending. No new nightly was
    triggered by these edits; CPU checks establish configuration consistency
    only.
    
    Use `/nightly GLM-5.3-W8A8C8-A3-200k-PP-PD` for the existing hardware
    workload. No new test files were added because this existing case
    supplies performance and AIME2025 coverage.
    
    ### Independent performance warmup
    
    Before the formal measurement, run 48 warmup requests from the same
    prefix0 16K GLM-5.3 dataset, concurrency 24, output length 1024, and
    request rate 1.4. The warmup baseline 0 is only a placeholder and is not
    regression evidence. Keep the formal 96-request baseline 877.3186 /
    threshold 0.97, AIME2025, topology and model options unchanged. This is
    intended to reduce first-request effects; coverage of all 16 Decode DP
    replicas and any improvement in variance still require worker logs and
    repeated hardware runs.
    
    Validation: parsed YAML, semantic comparison confirmed only the warmup
    case was added, verified benchmark order warmup/perf/accuracy, and
    rendered the 64-NPU server commands. git diff --check passed. Full
    format check was attempted but blocked by missing local pre-commit. No
    new nightly was triggered for this change.
    
    ### Warmed performance baseline calibration
    
    Commit `425f7c8be` sets the formal performance baseline to
    `min(1089.6467, 1122.6822) = 1089.6467 token/s` from the two latest runs
    with the independent 48-request warmup, and sets the threshold to `0.95`
    (gate `1035.164365 token/s`). Sources: run40834022871 (96/96 successful;
    original AISBench JSON verified) and run40859196273 (96/96 successful in
    live logs; raw artifact and final accuracy still pending at calibration
    time). These supersede the earlier formal baseline/threshold values in
    this description.
    
    The 48-request warmup, formal 96-request
    workload/concurrency24/rate1.4/output1024, AIME2025 and all server
    settings are unchanged. The currently running run40859196273 checked out
    `d74a71784` and still evaluates the prior `877.3186 * 0.97` gate; it
    does not validate this new calibration commit. Semantic YAML comparison,
    loader/rank/launch JSON checks and `git diff --check` passed. Required
    formatting was attempted but local pre-commit remains unavailable. No
    nightly was triggered.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542
    
